# Everything a friend needs to run Commit Roulette.
#
# Copy this file to apps/web/.env.local and fill it in. Vite only reads
# variables prefixed with VITE_. Every VITE_ value ends up in the browser
# bundle, so only publishable/anon keys may appear here.
#
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
#
# The three browser values are the only ones a frontend contributor needs.
# The function values are only needed if you are running the grader locally.

# =============================================================================
# 1. Clerk — the only identity provider
# =============================================================================
# Dashboard → API Keys → Publishable key. Starts with pk_test_ or pk_live_.
# Safe in the browser: it identifies the app, not a user.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_replace_me

# =============================================================================
# 2. Supabase — database, realtime, and the function host
# =============================================================================
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://replace-me.supabase.co

# Dashboard → Project Settings → API → anon public key. Starts with eyJ.
# Public by design. Safe in the browser ONLY because every table sits behind
# RLS. See docs/PLAN.md §4.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJreplace_me

# =============================================================================
# 3. Clerk dashboard setup (not a file, but the step everyone gets stuck on)
# =============================================================================
# Supabase → Authentication → Sign In / Providers → Third-party Auth → Clerk
#   → Add connection. Paste the Clerk issuer URL:
#       https://clerk.your-project.com
#   → Client ID: your Clerk Publishable key
#   → Client Secret: your Clerk Secret key
#   → Authorized email domains: your own domain
# Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Site URL: http://localhost:5173
#   → Redirect URLs: http://localhost:5173/**
#
# Clerk dashboard → Sessions → Customize session token → add to the claims:
#   {"postgres_role": "authenticated"}
# Without that claim Supabase treats every request as `anon` and RLS denies
# it. This is the single most common way to get "empty room, no error".
#
# Clerk dashboard → Sessions → Set the session token lifetime to 60 seconds.
# Realtime re-authorises on every heartbeat (default 25s), so a token that
# outlives its socket is fine but a token that expires faster than the
# heartbeat is not.

# =============================================================================
# 4. Grader — only needed to run execute-submission locally
# =============================================================================
# Judge0 CE. The public endpoint needs no key; leave this blank for that.
# A self-hosted Judge0 or a RapidAPI plan needs one.
JUDGE0_ENDPOINT=https://ce.judge0.com
JUDGE0_API_KEY=

# Judge0 limits. These are the defaults in _shared/judge0.ts.
JUDGE0_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
JUDGE0_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=400

# NEVER put your Clerk secret key or your Supabase service_role key in this
# file, or in any VITE_ variable. The function reads them from its own
# environment, set with `supabase secrets set`.
